  "id": "DrugBank_DB13943 - MONDO_9047",
  "verbalization": "Testosterone Cypionate, through its indication for Trisomy 13, is linked to Fluoxymesterone, which in turn is linked to Cryptorchidism. This suggests a potential pathway where Testosterone Cypionate may influence the development of Cryptorchidism via the Trisomy 13 pathway. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Trisomy 13 in both Testosterone Cypionate and Fluoxymesterone, indicating a possible role in the pathophysiology of the disease. The mechanism is likely mediated through the hormonal effects of Testosterone, as Fluoxymesterone is a testosterone analog that is known to influence testicular development. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential link between Testosterone Cypionate and Cryptorchidism, possibly through the indirect influence of testosterone on reproductive development.",
